===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|chemistry}} Of or relating to [[tungsten]], especially [[hexavalent]] tungsten.
#* {{quote-journal|year=1799|author=Cit. Guyton|title=Experiments on the Colouring Matter of Vegetable Juices with the Tungstic Acid|editor={{w|Alexander Tilloch}}|journal={{w|Philosophical Magazine}}|volume=IV|number=XIII|location=London|publisher=J. Davis|page=81|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/s1philosophicalm04lond#page/81|passage=Having ſubjected to experiment an oxyd hitherto little known, I mean the '''tungſtic''' oxyd, I ſoon diſcovered that it is one of the moſt valuable ſubſtances for receiving and fixing vegetable colours.}}
#* {{quote-book|year=1799|author={{w|Thomas Beddoes}}|title=Contributions to Physical and Mental Knowledge, Principally from the West of England|location=Bristol|publisher=Biggs & Cottle|page=120|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=d3EFAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA120#v=onepage&q&f=false|passage=The '''tungſtic''' phoſoxyd (yellow oxyd of tungſten) appears to contain light in its compoſition. It gives out phoſoxygen, and becomes blue on expoſure to ſolar light. It appears capable of combining with the alkalies, alkaline earths, &c.}}
#* {{quote-book|year=1924|author={{w|Zay Jeffries}}|author2=Robert Samuel Archer|title=The Science of Metals|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=rB1LAAAAMAAJ|publisher=McGraw–Hill|page=106|passage=[[thoria|Thoria]] is introduced as thorium nitrate into the '''tungstic''' oxide before the latter is reduced by hydrogen to tungsten power.}}

